      "worked_solution": "The measure of $∠POQ$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠POS)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠QOS).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠POQ={140}^{∘}-{95}^{∘}={45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/94c67d7c4920f05641ee469cafceeb8b9dfe453ff19f80afd882a806afabbac5.png)\n\n   \n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠POR:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠POR & =m∠POQ+m∠QOR \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}+{65}^{∘} \\\\  & ={110}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
